EVIDENCE:
{evidence}

Where could {technology} create value for Tata Communications in the {fabric_name} fabric?
FABRIC: {fabric_definition}
TATA TODAY: {tcl_today}
THIS FABRIC'S TWO LEVERS AND ITS KEY METRICS (use the lever ids):
{fabric_levers}
MECHANISMS (use their ids):
{mechanisms}
CAUTIONS: {fabric_cautions}
BLOCKERS TO TEST IN THIS FABRIC:
{fabric_blockers}

1. Name up to 2 use cases the pages support, highest impact first, citing pages by their [n] numbers. Don't invent.
   Title each one (and each suggestion) in plain words a business reader outside Tata understands, in under 20 words: what it does and for whom. Name a Tata product only beside what it is ("on Vayu, Tata's cloud"); spell out acronyms ("security operations centre", not "SOC").
2. Give every use case exactly two levers, in this order: lever 1, this fabric's contribution lever; lever 2, its delivery-cost lever. Give each lever the mechanism through which it creates value, from the list.
3. Write each lever as a chain: operating change → metric → financial effect → evidence needed → next step when. Take the metric from this fabric's key metrics where one fits. Cite the pages for each lever. Where the pages don't support a lever, still give it: leave its pages empty and say in "evidence_needed" what would show it.
4. Give the capital required for every use case, even when neither lever is about capital: light, moderate or heavy, and why in words, such as "light: software on the existing network".
5. From the blockers to test listed above, name any the pages show could stop it scaling in this fabric: the blocker's name exactly as listed, one plain sentence on why, the words from the page that show it, and the page's [n] number. Leave the list empty when the pages show none; don't guess.

Rules:
- compare equivalent outcomes at comparable quality;
- include implementation, integration, monitoring, exceptions and support costs;
- count customer savings as Tata value only through a fee, more demand or retention;
- keep retained contribution separate from new wins;
- for a protection lever, the value is the difference in loss rates with and without the technology, not the whole installed base;
- net off any revenue Tata already earns that the use case would displace;
- never write a figure: no revenue, margin, price, percentage, count of money or payback period. Say what would be measured, not how much.

If the pages show no use case: give "no_use_case" with what evidence would show one, and leave use_cases empty. You may then suggest up to 2 use cases from your own knowledge in "suggested", without citations.

Reply with ONLY a JSON object: {{"use_cases": [{{"title": "", "rank": 1, "pages": [n], "levers": [{{"lever_id": "lever 1's id", "mechanism_id": "", "operating_change": "", "metric": "", "financial_effect": "", "evidence_needed": "", "next_step_when": "", "pages": [n]}}, {{"lever_id": "lever 2's id", ...the same fields}}], "capital": {{"direction": "light|moderate|heavy", "why": ""}}}}], "no_use_case": null or {{"reason": "", "evidence_needed": ""}}, "suggested": [{{"title": "", "why": ""}}], "blockers": [{{"name": "a blocker exactly as listed", "why": "", "quote": "the words on the page", "page": n}}]}}

EVIDENCE:
{evidence}
